Vercel preview deployments use dynamic URLs (`frontend-{hash}-cliffs-projects-a84c76c9.vercel.app`) that weren't in the static CORS allowlist, causing CORS failures and white screens.

## Changes

- **`backend/app/core/environment.py`**: Added `is_valid_vercel_preview_origin()` with regex pattern to validate Vercel preview URLs for this project

- **`backend/app/main.py`**: Replaced static `CORSMiddleware` with custom middleware that:
  - Validates both static origins and dynamic Vercel previews
  - Returns 403 for disallowed origins on OPTIONS preflight
  - Adds CORS headers only for allowed origins

```python
# Validates Vercel preview URLs matching this project
VERCEL_PROJECT_PATTERN = re.compile(
    r'^https://frontend-[a-z0-9]+-cliffs-projects-a84c76c9\.vercel\.app$'
)

def is_valid_vercel_preview_origin(origin: str) -> bool:
    if not origin:
        return False
    return bool(VERCEL_PROJECT_PATTERN.match(origin))
```

